//! Counters keyed by a proven identity: a rate over a sliding window and a
//! quota over a day.
//!
//! The gateway throttles by address when it does not know who is asking.
//! Once a crawler is verified or an agent's signature checks out, the address
//! stops being the right key: one agent arrives from many addresses, and many
//! agents share one. These counters are keyed by the identity instead.
//!
//! Everything is held in this process, in bounded memory.
//!
//! FIXED BY THE PROJECT LEAD: DO NOT EDIT this file. Implement `engine.rs`
//! (and further private modules if you want them). Nothing may panic for any
//! input, and no input may make memory grow past the bound.
//!
//! # Identities
//!
//! An identity is any string, of any length and content. It is reduced to a
//! 128-bit keyed hash of the **whole** string (never a prefix), so its length
//! does not affect memory and two different identities do not share a
//! counter. At most `max_identities` are tracked. When a new one arrives and
//! the table is full, the identity used least recently (by order of calls to
//! [`Quotas::allow_rate`] and [`Quotas::take`], not by clock) is forgotten;
//! if it comes back it starts afresh. Memory is therefore at most
//! `max_identities` entries of `window_slots` 32-bit counters plus a few
//! words each.
//!
//! # Time
//!
//! Time is whole Unix seconds, passed in by the caller. A `now` earlier than
//! one already seen (by any call on this value) is treated as the latest time
//! seen, so a clock stepping backwards never hands anything back.
//!
//! **Rate.** Time is cut into slots of `slot_secs`. The window at `now` is
//! the `window_slots` slots ending with the slot that contains `now`
//! (slot number = `now / slot_secs`). With the defaults that is one minute
//! in ten-second steps.
//!
//! **Day.** The day at `now` is `now / day_secs`. A day's use belongs to that
//! day number alone: it is untouched by anything the rate window does and is
//! dropped only when a call arrives in a later day (or the identity is
//! forgotten as described above).
//!
//! # Snapshots
//!
//! [`Quotas::export`] and [`Quotas::import`] carry the day's use across a
//! restart, so that a restart does not give every identity a fresh day.
//! Rate windows are not carried: they last a minute. The identity hash key
//! is carried with them, because a new process draws a new key and would
//! otherwise find nothing it loaded. Format (version 1):
//!
//! ```text
//! version   u8 = 1
//! key       [u8; 16]          the identity hash key
//! day_secs  u64 big-endian
//! day       u64 BE            the day number the counts belong to
//! count     u32 BE
//! entries   count times: identity hash u128 BE, used u32 BE
//! ```
//!
//! Entries are the identities with something taken in that day, least
//! recently used first, no hash twice, `used` above 0, and nothing follows
//! the last one.

mod engine;

use std::fmt;

pub use engine::Quotas;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Config {
    pub slot_secs: u64,
    pub window_slots: u32,
    pub day_secs: u64,
    /// Most identities tracked at once.
    pub max_identities: usize,
    /// Key for the identity hash. `None` draws a random one per process,
    /// which is what a gateway wants; tests fix it to be repeatable.
    pub hash_seed: Option<[u8; 16]>,
}

impl Default for Config {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Config {
            slot_secs: 10,
            window_slots: 6,
            day_secs: 86_400,
            max_identities: 10_000,
            hash_seed: None,
        }
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ConfigError {
    /// `slot_secs`, `window_slots`, `day_secs` or `max_identities` is zero.
    Zero,
    /// `slot_secs` above 3600, `window_slots` above 60 or `max_identities`
    /// above 1,000,000.
    TooLarge,
}

impl fmt::Display for ConfigError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        f.write_str(match self {
            ConfigError::Zero => {
                "slot_secs, window_slots, day_secs and max_identities must not be zero"
            }
            ConfigError::TooLarge => "slot_secs, window_slots or max_identities too large",
        })
    }
}

impl std::error::Error for ConfigError {}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum SnapshotError {
    /// Not version 1, the wrong length for its count, a hash twice, or a
    /// `used` of 0.
    Malformed,
    /// Made with another `day_secs`.
    Mismatch,
    /// This value already tracks identities; a snapshot is loaded at start.
    NotEmpty,
}

impl fmt::Display for SnapshotError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        f.write_str(match self {
            SnapshotError::Malformed => "quota snapshot is malformed",
            SnapshotError::Mismatch => "quota snapshot was made with another day length",
            SnapshotError::NotEmpty => "quota snapshot can only be loaded before any use",
        })
    }
}

impl std::error::Error for SnapshotError {}
